# Notification, Transparency and Reporting

## 1. Internal Organisational Use

Any company, institution, organisation, or other legal entity intending to deploy or implement Wind Tunnel Lab for internal operational purposes must notify the copyright holder before such deployment or implementation.

Such notification must include:

- The legal name of the organisation.
- The responsible representative and contact information.
- The intended purpose and scope of use.
- The deployment environment.
- Whether the original or modified software will be used.
- The expected implementation date.

Permitted internal organisational use is royalty-free unless a separate written agreement establishes otherwise.

## 2. Commercial Use Notification

Any party seeking permission for commercial exploitation must obtain prior written authorization and execute a separate commercial licensing agreement before commencing the relevant activity.

The proposed commercial activity, monetisation model, revenue streams, and intended distribution method must be disclosed during the authorization process.

## 3. Recipient Transparency

Any party redistributing, modifying, or incorporating Wind Tunnel Lab into an authorised service must preserve the applicable copyright and licence notices.

Recipients must be clearly informed that Wind Tunnel Lab or a derivative component is incorporated into the software or service.

Where applicable, recipients must be provided access to the relevant licence terms and required source-code information.

## 4. Commercial Reporting

Commercial licensees must maintain accurate records of revenue attributable to their authorised exploitation of Wind Tunnel Lab.

Unless otherwise agreed in writing:

- Reporting shall occur quarterly.
- Reports shall be submitted within 30 days following the end of each calendar quarter.
- Payment shall be made within the same 30-day period, in accordance with the applicable commercial agreement.
- Reports must identify relevant revenue categories, deductions, calculations, and the resulting royalty amount.
- Records supporting royalty calculations must be retained for at least three years.

Zero-revenue periods must also be reported where the commercial agreement requires periodic reporting.

## 5. Verification and Audit

The copyright holder may request reasonable documentation to verify reported revenue and royalty calculations.

Any audit must be conducted with reasonable advance notice, during normal business hours, and subject to appropriate confidentiality obligations.

The scope and cost allocation of any independent audit may be specified in the relevant commercial agreement.

## 6. Payment and Taxation

Royalty rates, payment structures, currency, payment methods, applicable taxes, and other financial obligations shall be established in the relevant signed commercial agreement.

No universal royalty percentage is established by this licence.

## 7. Non-Compliance

Failure to satisfy applicable notification, reporting, payment, or commercial authorization requirements may result in suspension or termination of the relevant commercial permission, subject to applicable law and the terms of the agreement.

